# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Oxygen CODEOWNERS  —  every area has a PRIMARY and a BACKUP owner
#
# Convention: each rule lists two handles, `path  @primary  @backup`.
#   * @primary = the reliable owner (drove the area / knows it best).
#   * @backup  = second reviewer, covers when the primary is out.
# GitHub requests BOTH and lets EITHER approve — the order encodes the convention
# for humans; it does not change GitHub's behavior. Rules are matched
# last-match-wins, so the fine-grained overrides at the BOTTOM take precedence.
#
#   Handle            Person   Primary area
#   ----------------  -------  --------------------------------------------------
#   @luong-komorebi   Luong    Platform · custom apps · admin · authz · fleet · CI
#   @haitrr           Hai      Semantic model · world model · metrics & monitoring
#   @hotay            Tay      Cameras/video · airhouse · airway · agentic runtime
#   @nresh            Nick     Web shell · onboarding · browser tests · sources
#   @NTtanh           Mars     Billing · multi-tenancy · secrets · IDE/git · client shell
#
# Onboarding map + what each area is: internal-docs/team-ownership-matrix.md
# Kept current weekly by .github/workflows/ownership-matrix-refresh.yaml, which
# runs .github/scripts/ownership_analysis.py over the full commit history and
# opens a PR. Edit that script's PEOPLE/AREAS when the team or layout changes.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


